    the id being that line, on a non-empty probe file and on an unchanged line count
    (lines_before=149 lines_after=149, probe_len=464, read back from the file). boardctl create
    had written an empty `probe` key, which reads as filed; the bind replaces it.
    
    Events: 276 (task_created, CF-175) and 277 (audit, task CF-099). This tick's events were
    renumbered past a sibling's while rebasing onto 80c47cb — the review lane minted its own event
    275 in the same window, so both sides' lines are kept, the sibling keeps 275 and mine moved to
    276/277. After resolution: 277 events, 277 unique ids, 0 conflict markers, every line parses.
    
    The audit event records this tick: the four countable contradictions corrected in c1896cc, the
    measured gates, the two rows observed but deliberately not fixed (CF-155's premise is dead at
    this tip; CF-049 is live — the canonical checkout still carries a stale REBASE_HEAD), and what
    was not run.
    
