 {"id":"CF-173","title":"P3 \u2014 the layer-00 reach probe reports 000 (unreachable) for a URL that answered 200: the CF-037 fix shape discards curl's printed code when --max-time cuts the transfer","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T07:35:13Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T07:35:13Z","detail":{"lane":"code-factory-dogfood","tick":"code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-04-07-25-03","evidence":"~/.hermes/stand-in/dogfood/code-factory/dogfood-2026-11-04-evidence.md#3"},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 at published tip eada934 with a portable fixture (no external network): a local `python3 -m http.server` serving a 100 KB body, probed with `curl --limit-rate 20k --max-time 1`. Result: `curl_printed_code=200 curl_rc=28 script_value=000`. scripts/project-node.sh:190-195 (the shape CF-037 introduced) is `if ! c=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 8 \"$u\" 2>/dev/null); then c=000; fi`: curl writes the status it already received (200) and then exits 28 when --max-time cuts the body, and the `if !` throws that printed value away and records 000. The FAIL row then reads `reach:<url> \u2014 -> 000`, which is indistinguishable from DNS failure or no egress. Observed in the wild on 2026-11-03's node: layer 00 printed `FAIL reach:https://pypi.org/simple/ \u2014 -> 000` in the same run whose layer 40 printed `PASS repo_clone \u2026 @ df40870`, and three direct probes on that node returned http=200 at 9.4-10.0 s, aborted mid-body. A stranger's next move is to chase DNS or egress on a node that just cloned over the same network, and the FAIL names no value to supply. Distinct from CF-037 (the `|| echo 000` deformation, fixed) and CF-072 (that deformation in three other scripts): this is the replacement idiom's false-negative mode, and it fires on a REACHABLE URL.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the pre-fix tree from the repo root: `port=18932; d=$(mktemp -d); dd if=/dev/zero of=\"$d/big\" bs=1k count=100 status=none; ( cd \"$d\" &&